// lexicon-child-en — curated, frequency-tagged child lexicon for the game-based WORD types
// (GB-WORDFORGE-01 "Word Forge", GB-WORDLADDER-01 "Letter Climb").
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
// Both types are deterministically checkable ONLY against a fixed word list: a word
// ladder is a shortest-path search over the lexicon graph, and a forge rack's answer key
// is the exact set of lexicon words spellable from the rack. Depending on a system
// dictionary (/usr/share/dict/words) or a network fetch would make generation and
// checking non-reproducible and would drag in adult/obscure vocabulary that a child
// cannot be expected to know. So the word list is embedded in the repo.
//
// CURATION RULES
//  - Concrete, age-appropriate, everyday English. No proper nouns, no abbreviations,
//    no hyphenates, no words a screener should not put in front of a child.
//  - Every word is tagged with a VOCABULARY BAND 1..7 (7 = earliest / most frequent,
//    1 = rare / above-level). The band is a DESIGN ESTIMATE in the Zipf-like convention
//    already used by the verbal generators in this directory (VER-WORDTRAIN-01,
//    VER-BUILDIT-01) — it is NOT a corpus measurement and is not calibrated.
//  - The band is what makes `M-VOCABLVL` derivable server-side (rarest band reached) and
//    what lets the reading-load gate (D-017) keep the bottom of the difficulty ramp to
//    short, high-frequency words a beginning reader can actually decode.
//
// Lengths 3..5 carry the ladder graph (one-letter-change neighbours). Lengths 6..7 exist
// so a forge rack can afford long/rare words at the top of the ramp.
//
// Governance: born-synthetic content. Vocabulary bands are provisional design estimates
// (RES-012/RES-013); nothing here is validated against child data.

import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';

